# Technical documentation

Technical docs live in `docs/technical/en.md` and `docs/technical/fa.md`. They describe how the app is built: stack, setup, routes, auth, data, storage, and server behavior. Business meaning stays in `docs/business/`.

When a code change adds, removes, or alters setup, dependencies, routes, auth, schema, storage, APIs, or behavior these docs describe, update both technical files in the same change:

- Keep the same facts in both languages. Wording may differ; meaning may not.
- Update the "Last updated" date in both files.
- Name the real paths, tables, env vars, and limits. Do not describe a planned design as if it already exists.
- If the UI and the database disagree, document both.
- Skip only edits that do not change anything the technical docs describe, such as a comment or a color.

A user-facing change still follows `.cursor/rules/business-docs.mdc` as well.

```md
<!-- ❌ BAD: a new API route is merged and only en.md mentions it -->
<!-- ✅ GOOD: both technical docs list the route, who can call it, and what it writes -->
```
